  sure that there will be more and more  applications developed for iPhone iPad  or Android or whatever which to me is  quite revolutionary so someone came on  and said that these iPads are a  distraction that essentially you have to  have that face-to-face interaction  between the teacher and the learner in  order for learning to take place and so  we've had quite a lively exchange and so  I guess the question comes up you know  what is the future role of a classroom  or a teacher insofar as language  learning is concerned so let me say that  you know I have often said that I  believe that massive input is almost a  precondition for being able to learn  grammar that without this exposure to  the language the grammar explanations  don't stick I've said that it's very  difficult and I'm this is based on my  experience as a learner and watching  other people learn it's very difficult  to learn these rules and study some a  few words and try and put them together  because all of these grammar concepts  take a long time to sink in and it  requires a lot of exposure and  experience with the language before  these explanations start to make sense  and start to stick and therefore my  preference is to focus on listening and  reading vocabulary accumulation so that  I have a more solid base in  comprehension so that I can understand  the language I don't worry about  speaking for six months per year  depending on the language and I find  that when I start to speak or if I have  a need to speak the bigger my vocabulary  the more familiar I am with the language  the better I understand what I hear the  better I do so then what is the rule of  the class what is the role of the  classroom well the role of the classroom  is not going to go away because most  people aren't motivated enough to learn  on their own most people believe that  they can only learn in the classroom so  the idea that there are all these  resources available on the Internet is  relatively new I find that the  explanations of  I can find them all over the internet so  I don't have to sit in the classroom and  hope that the issue that I have  difficulty with is the one that the  teacher is gonna focus on that day I can  zoom in on those issues that I'm  interested in so however now I want to  backtrack and say that add link I would  say that the best tutors are people who  are professional teachers teachers okay  that's whether it be you know if Jenny  and in in st. Petersburg but it would be  Reinhard in Vienna and I'm not gonna  name everybody but you know even in  Sofia you know and I deal with I deal  with a lot of tutors and so that's the  second issue I need tutors once I have  spent enough time with the language be  at six months or more then I need to  talk to tutors I need the tutors to  point out my mistakes I have to  sometimes ask them questions what also  happens in the case of link you have  tutors who create content about  different issues of grammar and put them  in our library so we can review them  over and over again we can listen to  them in the target language whether it  be various content in German or evgeny's  in Russian or whomever I can listen to  it over and over again so I'm listening  and reading and also focusing on those  grammar issues that I'm ready to focus  on that I want to focus on so the role  of the teacher remains important the  role of the teacher first of all as a  stimulus because if I know that I'm  going to be talking to my tutor it kind  of keeps me going I want to show my  tutor that I'm improving the tutor is  very often a source of encouragement a  source of stimulus but it's not so much  a matter of explaining things that's the  thing that the teacher as explainer I  just don't see that as such an important  role because the third theoretical  explanation is not gonna do it you have  to see the patterns over and over again  refer over and over again perhaps to  some grammar rules where the learner has  the initiative and so in our exchange of  course with this person on the  you know the iPad and language learning  or something like that in fact I might  put a link to that particular video I  mean he was on and on about how if you  don't cover the classroom you can learn  because it's very difficult because  there's five different future tenses I  mean yeah you can make the language  sound as complicated as you want I don't  think anyone can absorb five future  tenses at one city but if a learner  hasn't had enough exposure to the  language bit by bit  by reviewing certain grammar rules  either on their own or by having their  writing or their conversational language  corrected they'll start to notice these  things more and more so many people tell  me at length that they have learned much  more with us than they have in a more  traditional classroom setting that's not  to condemn the teacher I think there are  lots of excellent teachers but in a  classroom with fifteen or twenty other  students the teacher decides the agenda  and I think that the learner needs to  decide the agenda and the learner needs  to control their learning and I suspect  that what's going to happen is that what  we are doing at Linc  oh and of course the other thing that  people like to criticize me for is that  I'm just out promoting and pushing you  know this product that I'm selling and  stuff like that of course I'm promoting  link but why did I create link in the  first place because I think is helpful  to language learning now of course we  have a lot of cost that makes the work  obviously interested in encouraging  people to come and use it and the more  people who come and use it the more we  can invest in making it better that's no  different than the commercial interests  that a teacher has or an ESL school has  in promoting their form of language  instruction services it's a saint and we  are ultimately what matters the most is  where is the best return on investment  for the language learner in other words  is the language learner better off going  to an ESL school say the person wants to  learn English say jump on a flat plane  from Japan or  fly to Vancouver enroll in an ESL school  that's $1200 a month and stay in a  homestay and do all of these things is  that a good return on investment  ultimately that's what's going to matter  and that the market will decide that I  think that it's not ideal I think that a  smaller number of instructional hours a  smaller number of hours of interaction  three hours a week five hours a week  would be very heavy in my opinion one  two three hours a week with a tutor  either online or face-to-face and then  some encouragement from the tutor or  some explanation on how to learn  directing the tutor to where is a  learner rather to where they can find  excellent resources that's a better use  of the teachers time better return on  investment for the learner and it would  enable teachers to reach many many more  people in the case of Canada  I mean immigrants apparently we spend  $3,000 per head per year on immigrant  language training and a recent study out  of Toronto showed that at least amongst  the Chinese speaking immigrants who are  the largest source country in Canada  after seven years a group of 3,000 of  these immigrants were followed and they  were enrolled in language programs here  and they made essentially no progress no  progress the sort of another group the  Slavic speakers did make progress and  the reason to make progress is because  they were more likely to make friends  with Canadians interact more with  Canadians take a greater interest in the  local culture in other words what  mattered the most was what they did  outside the classroom not what they did  inside the classroom so that being the  case why spend three thousand dollars a  year per immigrant or twelve hundred  dollars a month for these ESL programs  when there are more cost-effective ways  that you can utilize teacher resources  and after all it's only a small  percentage of immigrants that are helped  through these language programs many  more are unable to get into these  programs so why wouldn't we devise a  more efficient way to enable teachers to  help learners or to encourage learners  to hell  to learn on their own and I think in  that regard the iPad iPhone other mobile  devices Android art and the Internet and  all the resources that are on the  Internet are revolutionary and they have  changed the paradigm and so to continue  to insist that language instruction can  only take place in the classroom as this  Tiki whatever is doing he alternates  between that and you know getting vulgar  and insulting me you know to me that's I  understand the guy he wants to protect  his job that's fine plus that's perhaps  all he knows but the reality is that  that there are so many other resources  available today that didn't exist ten  even ten years ago let alone 50 years  ago so there you have it I thought I  would just you know and he's welcome to  make a video and post it here as a  response I haven't deleted any of this  even though they're everything kind of a  bit nasty I haven't deleted any of his  comments yeah I think free exchange of  ideas and it's not and I repeat this  it's not an T teacher I think there are  while there are some teachers who are  protectionist of their position and  closed-minded I know a lot of teachers  who are looking for new resources  looking for ways to do their job better  who want to help more people some of  them are members of link some of them  are the best tutors that we have but I  think that and I also recognize that in  a you know public school environment a  large number of students are not very  motivated and therefore the teacher's  job really is to push the curriculum at  them and force them to take tests and  hope that most of the past and of course  if we look at the results in Canada even  where many do pass say they're French  very few of them learn how to speak the  language so there is something  fundamentally wrong with what we're  doing in the way languages are taught in  the school system and I think to  basically dismiss the iPad and mobile  devices is some kind of a distraction  you know promoted by the crass  commercialism of Apple and examples of  this sort of out-of-control consumerism  in the modern world it's not like that  to me it defeats the purpose the issue  is can they be  effectively to augment and to you know  what is done by the teacher to empower  the learner to empower the teacher I  think the answer is yes so there you  have it thank you for listening

